From: Rohan <kharade@eurecom.fr>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:43:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(smf): release and report QoS flows the NG-RAN refuses

A PCF-initiated PDU Session Modification (TS 23.502 4.3.3.2) adds the QoS
flows at the UPF before the NG-RAN is asked; the NG-RAN may refuse them in its
PDU Session Resource Modify Response (step 4): the whole session (Modify
Unsuccessful Transfer, PDU_RES_MOD_FAIL) or single flows (QoS Flow Failed to
Add or Modify List of the Modify Response Transfer, TS 38.413 9.3.4.2). Until
now the SMF ignored both and the UPF kept marking the traffic with a QFI the
NG-RAN has no bearer for: it was dropped (e.g. srsUE, which supports one QoS
flow only).

- The flows added by a PCF-initiated modification stay pending until the
  NG-RAN answers.
- Refused flows are removed at the UPF (N4 Session Modification: Remove
  PDR/FAR/QER) without N1/N2, their QFI and IDs freed: the traffic is back on
  the session's QoS flows.
- Their PCC rules are reported to the PCF in Npcf_SMPolicyControl_Update
  (ruleReports: ruleStatus INACTIVE, failureCode RES_ALLO_FAIL; TS 29.512
  4.2.4.1, 5.6.2.7) and removed from the SMF's decision.
- The AMF gets 204 No Content once the UPF has removed them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
